---
metadata: {
    partial_name: "Emails | Sender",
}
---
{%- comment -%}
  Who this app's emails come from. Called with:
    function sender = 'emails/sender'
  Returns { "name": ..., "email": ..., "reply_to": ..., "ok": true|false }.

  The address is the instance's verified sender, from the CRM module: the customer's own
  domain once it is verified in Insites Console, otherwise no-reply@insites.site. Mail is
  never sent from an address the instance cannot authenticate, because a customer domain
  that is not verified fails delivery checks (SPF, DKIM, DMARC) and the mail is dropped.
  The display name is company_name from CMS Globals, and replies go to company_email_1
  from CMS Globals. Without company_email_1 the mail still goes, with no Reply-To.
  ok is false only when the instance has no sendable sender at all (for example a
  suspended instance). Pages that send email check it and say email is not available.
  The partials named here come from the installed CRM and CMS modules, which the linter
  cannot see.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}insites-check-disable-next-line MissingPartial{%- endcomment -%}
{%- include 'modules/insites_cms/globals' -%}
{%- comment -%}insites-check-disable-next-line MissingPartial{%- endcomment -%}
{%- function resolved = 'modules/insites_crm/functions/email_sender/resolve' -%}
{%- comment -%}insites-check-disable-next-line MissingPartial{%- endcomment -%}
{%- function customer = 'modules/insites_crm/functions/email_sender/customer_sender', sender: resolved -%}
{%- liquid
  assign global = context.exports.global
  assign sender = {}
  assign sender['name'] = global.company_name | default: customer.name | default: '' | strip
  assign sender['email'] = customer.address | default: '' | strip
  assign sender['reply_to'] = global.company_email_1 | default: '' | strip
  assign sender['ok'] = false
  if customer.is_sendable == true and sender.email != blank
    assign sender['ok'] = true
  else
    log 'Seedling cannot send email: this instance has no sendable sender. Check its email sender in Insites Console.', type: 'error'
  endif
  return sender
-%}
